    T44
        title       The suite judges from its own facts only, gated by machines
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T43]
        description
            No path leads from a runtime report to an obligation, enforced by type and lint, and machine gates run
            on every checkpoint.

            **Why now:** six reviews found the same class, a report deciding an obligation; the advisor's Q1, Q6,
            Q7 and Q9 replace instance fixes with a structural rule and gates.

            **Read first:** code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/advisor-answers-2026-11-11.md (Q0, Q1, Q6, 
            Q7, Q9); code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/dsl/oracle.ts.

            **Approach:** split `Fact` so obligation code cannot see a report, with a lint ban; a liar gate (a
            mutant's acts with a correct runtime's recorded reports must stay red); a diffed catch matrix; generic
            mutants of `src/core` (a two-hour StrykerJS trial, else a small operator mutator); a crash generator; a
            generated gate file that notes and reports cite instead of hand-copied numbers.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, lint configuration, `package.json` scripts.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments; the generated gate file.
            - **False pass:** a report path left open → caught by the liar gate.
        acceptance
            - obligation code takes no runtime report (type and lint enforced);
            - under the liar gate no behavioural mutant turns green;
            - catch matrix, core mutants, crash generator and gate file run on every checkpoint.
