        title       Suite phase-out, first cut: Pay and Cells generated, hand traces thinned
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T47]
        description
            Pay and Cells become generated parts in the top-level `fixtures/`; Pay's hand rows stay as one frozen
            golden; the hand traces give way to the model search (phase-out step 4).

            **Why now:** the user accepted the phase-out (2026-11-11), including Pay as a generated part, which reverses
            replan decision 5 ("Pay is not converted") for Pay. Without this cut the suite keeps two descriptions of
            Pay and two judges of every run.

            **Read first:** code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/conformance-phase-out-2026-11-11.md (step 4,
            validations V1 to V4), @task.V3.T47, @task.V3.T45, @spec.Conformance.R15.

            **Approach:** `machines/pay.ts` and `pay.contracts.ts` move to `fixtures/pay/`; Pay gains a user model and a
            server model (about 30 lines) and declares its `classify`; `referenceOf` replaces `fixtures/pay.ts` for
            every runtime, round-14 included; Pay's hand rows and handler table stay as one frozen golden static case
            (about 300 lines); `fixture.ts` becomes the real-fixture registry and `dsl/actor.ts` types the view from the
            definition's Schemas; traces whose cells the search reaches are deleted, and a kept trace names its ruling;
            the step-mutant list gives way to cell mutation; `not-yet.ts`'s remaining rows become matrix rows and the
            file is deleted; Pay's hand cases thin where a generated run or kept case catches the same mutants. Effort
            about 1.5 (estimate).

            **Gap:** the five scenario files that hold checks only case expectations make wait for an oracle or the
            model (here or @task.V3.T45); their cases stay until then.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, `packages/flow-state-v3/fixtures/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a derived reference that copies a compiler bug → caught by the frozen golden and the
              Compile static cases.
            - **Gates:** falsify on round-14 and production; matrix and coverage; `nub run check`.
        acceptance
            - Pay and Cells run as generated parts from `fixtures/pay/`; Pay's hand rows remain as one frozen golden.
            - `referenceOf` equals the hand rows for Pay and Cells (rows, handlers, schedules, every operation field,
              `classify`) before any deletion.
            - `not-yet.ts` and the deleted traces are gone; every hand-listed step mutant is still killed, by the search
              or by a kept trace.
            - Phase-out checks (the four validations): no lost catch in the catch matrix; the same coverage and
              feature-matrix rows; the derived reference equal to the hand rows wherever both exist;
              Compile static cases green on each fixture's `Compiled`.
